<title>FRANCE: SCOR sees no flood impact on 97 results.</title>
<headline>SCOR sees no flood impact on 97 results.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>French re-insurance company SCOR said on Thursday that it estimated losses resulting from floods in central Europe at $10-$12 million.</p>
<p>As that amount fits into normal business expense, SCOR does not expect the floods to have an impact on 1997 results, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;This disaster is not of an exceptional nature and will not have an impact on results foreseen for the year,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
